  "claims": [
    "Existing rewrite tracks and supplied higher cells interpret as endpoint equalities for the single shared-state evaluator; arbitrary correlated past and initial state/input are retained.",
    "Starting from a universally stateful checked original MAC root, the old structural catalogue and both suffix completions are checked in the same base model using explicit expansion into old proof tracks.",
    "A single Sum-labelled catalogue combines existing checked roots with all 18 cartesian pure-wire laws.",
    "Wire normalization generates an actual 18-law track in the unified catalogue, with empty root support and exact surrounding-context support.",
    "Existing local higher generators, pure local generators, and separated two-step cross exchanges form an explicit partial unified basis. Old higher proofs retain exact support and constructor counts; pure higher proofs retain zero support and exact counts.",
    "Four added local higher schemata exchange one actual cartesian wire step with left/right sequential/tensor wire fusion. Both boundaries contain two mixed steps; each higher root has one constructor and no guards.",
    "Arbitrary mixed placements retain one higher constructor and exactly the surrounding guard set, with stateful correlated-joint repair in the updated checked model.",
    "A concrete left-unit-inverse expansion instantiates a new fusion square; that pure change has no proof even with inverses using the old eleven pure-wire roots.",
    "The unified forward rewriting relation is not well founded: an actual infinite mixed copy-expansion chain is exhibited.",
    "A concrete original MAC checked interpretation of the unified rule catalogue retains the additional shared state as analysis context."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The original MAC root must be proved universally in the whole shared state; structural extension does not infer root validity from distributions without state.",
    "Endpoint kernel equality is already obtained from one track. These higher repair theorems do not establish a higher-dimensional necessity or proof-size advantage.",
    "The unified basis is partial: fixed-structure, nested/root-root and other cross critical overlaps are not exhaustively classified or filled.",
    "Completeness of the 18-law pure-wire equality presentation is not completeness of the higher basis or of mixed game equality.",
    "The four schemas have arbitrary typed wiring/context payload; one higher constructor or two boundary steps does not bound total bytes or checking time.",
    "The pure old-eleven-root obstruction is not a new global nonderivability theorem for every old mixed catalogue.",
    "The recursive pure-wire normalizer does not imply termination of unrestricted rewriting; no terminating-rewriting coherence theorem is applied unconditionally.",
    "The concrete original MAC interpretation is analysis-only on the extra state; proof edits do not rerun a native caller.",
    "This stateful crypto/structural catalogue is distinct from the prior same-program native-chunk signature. Full mixed code extraction, quantitative error and runtime integration remain open.",
    "Native internal oracle costs, scalable cryptographic examples, fair total-cost comparison and primary-theorem novelty confirmation remain unfinished."
  ],
